Assembler Version 01
====================
Assembled by: Version 00

Features Supported by This Assembler
-------------------------------------
This is a single-pass assembler that introduces non-standard 6502 mnemonics,
labels, and operand types. It reads tokens from the input and looks up
mnemonics in a built-in instruction table using linear search.

Instruction mnemonics (non-standard syntax, addressing mode encoded in name):
  ADC# ADCZ ASLA BCC BCS BEQ BNE BRK CLC CMPZ,X CMP# CMP,Y DEY INCZ INX
  INY JMP JSR LDAZ LDA# LDA(),Y LDA,Y LDX# LDY# ORAZ RTS SBC# SEC STA
  STA(),Y STAZ STAZ,X TYA

DATA directive:
  DATA $XX ...        - emit hex bytes
  DATA "string"       - emit ASCII string literals with \n and \\ escapes
  DATA $XXXX          - emit 16-bit value (little-endian)
  Mixed: DATA $XX "string" $XXXX on same line

Operand types in instruction arguments:
  $XX                 - 8-bit hex value
  $XXXX               - 16-bit hex value (little-endian)
  "string"            - ASCII string with \n and \\ escape sequences
  label               - 16-bit label reference (little-endian)

Labels:
  - Labels are defined at column 0 (start of line, no leading whitespace)
  - Labels receive the current program counter value
  - Label lookup uses linear search through a label table at $3000
  - Forward references are NOT supported (single-pass)
  - Duplicate label detection with error

Error handling:
  - BRK with inline error code and message string
  - Error 01: Duplicate label
  - Error 02: Opcode not found
  - Error 03: Label not found

Semicolon comments (to end of line).
Output starts at $2000 (hardcoded).

New in this version (relative to version 00):
- Non-standard 6502 instruction mnemonics with built-in instruction table
- Labels defined at start of line (bound to program counter)
- Label references as 16-bit operands
- Hex operands ($XX and $XXXX) with automatic 1 or 2 byte emission
- String literal operands ("string") with escape sequences (\n, \\)
- DATA directive supporting mixed hex, string, and label arguments
- Error reporting via BRK with inline messages

Features Used in This Assembler's Source Code
----------------------------------------------
The source is written entirely in DATA directives with hex bytes, which is
the only feature version 00 supports. All 6502 instructions are manually
encoded as hex byte sequences. The instruction mnemonic table, subroutine
addresses, branch targets, and error messages are all encoded as raw hex
values. The reset vector entry point address is emitted as the final two
DATA bytes.

Source features used:
  - DATA $XX $XX ... (hex byte emission only)
  - Semicolon comments (documenting the intended mnemonics)

New source features (relative to version 00):
- None. The source uses the same DATA-with-hex-bytes format as version 00.
  The comments are more detailed, showing the equivalent mnemonic source,
  but these are still just comments.
